  "intro": "You already know مَا + past verb: مَا ذَهَبْتُ (I didn't go). The standard, more formal way is لَمْ + the present form of the verb, whose last vowel becomes a sukūn: أَذْهَبُ (I go) → لَمْ أَذْهَبْ (I didn't go). Add بَعْدُ at the end for 'not yet': لَمْ أَكْتُبِ الْوَاجِب بَعْدُ (I haven't written the homework yet).",
  "objectives": [
    "Say what you didn't do with لَمْ + the present form",
